! C22-6578 PROBLEM 2.3, "DELETION OF EVERY FIFTH BIT IN A FIELD",
! printed pp.14-15 (PDF 15-16), read in the ink.  Methods 1, 2, 3, 5, 6.
! Method 4 (decimal) is problem_2_3_method4.strap.
!
!   "Given a string of 60 bits starting at FIELD, delete every fifth bit
!   starting at FIELD +0.04 and put the 48 bit result consecutively
!   starting at FIEL.  Assume that there is no overlap between (FIELD -
!   FIELD +0.59) and (FIEL - FIEL +0.47)."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS are every line below that is not marked
! otherwise.  What the deck adds or changes, all of it marked:
!
!  * Labels.  The page reuses VFIELD/VFIEL/LOAD in each method; the deck
!    numbers the FIEL areas (FIEL1..FIEL8), the control words
!    (VFIEL1..VFIEL6) and the loop labels, so that every method runs in
!    one program on the one FIELD.  Method 1's BZXCZ, LOAD is printed;
!    Method 3's pairs "instead of LOADA and LOADA +1.0" get Method 2's
!    frame with the branch written $-2.0.
!  * No halt until the end: Method 2's printed BEW, $ is replaced by
!    falling into the next method (a CNOP keeps each one word-aligned,
!    which the printed $-1.0 depends on).
!  * FIELD's data, FIEL's initial contents.
!
! TWO PRINTED STATEMENTS ARE WRONG AS PRINTED, by the page's own text:
!
!  1. Method 2, "BZXCZ, $-1.0".  Method 3 says the L and the ST are at
!     "LOADA and LOADA +1.0", so the BZXCZ is at LOADA +2.0 and $-1.0 is
!     the ST, not the L.  As printed the loop stores the FIRST group
!     twelve times.  The deck runs it AS PRINTED (FIEL2, expected
!     FFFFFFFFFFFF, the first nibble twelve times) and again with $-2.0
!     (FIEL3, NOT PRINTED), which is the stated result.
!  2. Method 3, third pair, "ST(B,4,3) (V+I), 0.04($3)".  With (V+I) the
!     count in $3 is never touched, so the BZXCZ that closes the loop
!     never sees XCZ change.  Read at 200 dpi: the print is (V+I), where
!     the other two pairs and Methods 1-2 print (V+IC).  The deck runs
!     it with (V+IC), NOT PRINTED, and does not run the printed form
!     (it does not terminate).
!
! EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED from the problem statement and the
! Reference Manual, not taken from the model.  FIELD is twelve 5-bit
! groups; the four kept bits of each, in hex, then the deleted bit:
!
!     F/1 1/0 A/1 5/1 0/0 9/1 C/0 3/0 E/1 7/1 8/0 6/1
!
!   = F8AAB04F06EBE0D, and four 1s fill the word (F8AAB04F06EBE0DF) so a
! load that ran past bit 59 would show.  The answer is the kept nibbles,
! F1A509C3E786, in FIEL +0.0 to +0.47; FIEL +0.48 to +0.63 start as A5A5
! and must be left alone.  Every FIELn word ends F1A509C3E786A5A5, but
! FIEL2 (above).
!
! WHY EACH METHOD GIVES THAT (Reference Manual printed pages):
!
!  M1  L(B,5,1): a signed field with a one-bit sign byte (p.36 table:
!      byte size 1 is S alone), so the fifth bit is the SIGN and the
!      other four the magnitude; ST(BU,4) stores the magnitude.  The
!      deleted bits are 1 in seven groups, so the sign is exercised.
!  M2  L(BU,5), then ST(BU,4) at offset 1 drops the low-order bit.
!  M3  pair 1: load only four of the five.  Pair 2: (B,5,2) is a sign
!      byte S T (p.36), so three bits are magnitude, the fourth is the
!      sign and the fifth the T flag; ST(B,4,1) stores three bits and
!      the sign.  Pair 3: LWF(B,5,4) is one bit and S T U V; ST(B,4,3)
!      stores one bit and S T U -- LOAD WITH FLAG (p.61) because LOAD
!      would clear T and U, which here are data.
!  M5  Offset indexing, p.21: the second half's I "may be used to modify
!      bits 35-50 of the instruction ... bit position 3 of the index
!      word is aligned with bit position 35", so bit 18 of the value
!      field is one unit of offset, and that is the page's comment (a),
!      "5 units in the 19 bit address subfield".  Offsets 56, 51, ... 1.
!  M6  Connectives, pp.74-75: each 5-bit storage byte becomes an 8-bit
!      accumulator byte "by the addition of high-order zeros"; CM0101 at
!      offset 1 with byte size 4 truncates each result byte to four.
!
! Progressive indexing, p.21: the value field is the effective address
! and is then incremented; XCZ follows the new count.
!
! MEASURED, against a control of 10 of 10 (nine words and the halt PC):
!  * FIELD's last KEPT bit set (..E0DF -> ..E0FF): OBSERVED 8 fail -- M1,
!    M2_branch_corrected, the three M3, M5, M6 (each ...E787) and
!    FIELD_unchanged.  M2_as_printed passes, as it must: it never reads
!    past the first group.
!  * FIELD's last DELETED bit cleared (..E0DF -> ..E0CF): OBSERVED 1
!    fails, FIELD_unchanged alone.  No method's answer depends on a
!    deleted bit.

        SLC, 1000.0
! --- Method 1 ------------------------------------------------------
START   LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL1
LOAD    L(B, 5, 1) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(BU,4) (V+IC), 0.04($3)
        BZXCZ, LOAD
        CNOP
! --- Method 2, AS PRINTED: BZXCZ, $-1.0 ----------------------------
        LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL2
LOADA   L(BU, 5) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(BU, 4) (V+IC), 0.04($3), 1
        BZXCZ, $-1.0
        CNOP
! --- Method 2, branch address corrected to LOADA (not printed) -----
        LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL3
LOADB   L(BU, 5) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(BU, 4) (V+IC), 0.04($3), 1
        BZXCZ, $-2.0
        CNOP
! --- Method 3, first pair ------------------------------------------
        LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL4
LOADC   L(BU, 4) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(BU, 4) (V+IC), 0.04($3)
        BZXCZ, $-2.0
        CNOP
! --- Method 3, second pair -----------------------------------------
        LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL5
LOADD   L(B, 5, 2) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(B, 4,1) (V+IC), 0.04($3)
        BZXCZ, $-2.0
        CNOP
! --- Method 3, third pair, (V+I) corrected to (V+IC) (not printed) -
        LV, $2, VFIELD
        LX, $3, VFIEL6
LOADE   LWF(B,5,4) (V+I), 0.05($2)
        ST(B,4,3) (V+IC), 0.04($3)
        BZXCZ, $-2.0
        CNOP
! --- Method 5 ------------------------------------------------------
        LX, $1, XW1; LVI, $2, 56
        L(BU, 60), FIELD
STORE   ST(BU, 4) (V+I), 0.04($1), 0($2)
        V-I, $2, 5
        BZXVLZ, STORE
! --- Method 6 ------------------------------------------------------
        CNOP
        C0011 (BU, 60, 5), FIELD
        CM0101 (BU, 48, 4), FIEL8, 1
HALT    BEW, $

VFIELD  VF, FIELD
VFIEL1  XW, FIEL1, 12, $
VFIEL2  XW, FIEL2, 12, $
VFIEL3  XW, FIEL3, 12, $
VFIEL4  XW, FIEL4, 12, $
VFIEL5  XW, FIEL5, 12, $
VFIEL6  XW, FIEL6, 12, $
XW1     XW, FIEL7, 0, $

        SLC, 1200.0
GUARD   DD(BU,64,8), (16)0000000000000001
FIELD   DD(BU,64,8), (16)F8AAB04F06EBE0DF
FIEL1   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL2   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL3   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL4   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL5   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL6   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL7   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
FIEL8   DD(BU,64,8), (16)000000000000A5A5
        END, START
